---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const b = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const faqs = [
  ['How much does TaxDome cost?', 'TaxDome prices by active clients, billed annually. Pricing starts at 150 active clients for $1,500 a year (about $0.83 per client a month) and includes 20 seats. Firms under 150 still pay the 150-client minimum. Above 150, volume bands apply (TaxDome FAQ examples: 400 clients $4,125/yr; 1,000 $9,000/yr; 3,000 $16,500/yr). Optional add-ons: AI $200/mo, Managed Client Care $100/mo, Premium support $249/mo.'],
  ['Does TaxDome charge per seat?', 'No. The published plan includes 20 seats with no per-seat charge. Custom pricing (unlimited seats, SLA, white-label app, extended API) is quote-based for firms that need it.'],
  ['Which TaxDome alternative is cheapest for a 3-person, 20-client firm?', 'Among published prices, Financial Cents Team at 3 × $49 = $147 a month on annual billing, or $247 with the Month-End Close add-on for 20 clients. Karbon Team is 3 × $59 = $177 a month on annual billing. TaxDome at the 150-client minimum is $1,500 a year (~$125 a month). Double does not publish prices.'],
  ['When should a firm stay on TaxDome?', 'Stay if you also do tax work and want organizers, IRS transcripts and return delivery in the same portal, if you want clients to explain uncategorized QBO transactions in a Bookkeeping Hub without a separate per-client add-on, or if you want a branded client portal and mobile app and are fine paying annually.'],
];
const faqLd = JSON.stringify({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqs.map(([q, a]) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: a } })),
});
---
<Base
  title="TaxDome alternatives for bookkeeping firms: practice management with published prices"
  description="Options beyond TaxDome's per-active-client portal and Bookkeeping Hub: Karbon, Financial Cents and Double, with pricing verified Nov 2026 and cost for a 3-person, 20-client firm."
>
  <h1>TaxDome alternatives</h1>
  <p>TaxDome is practice management for tax and bookkeeping firms: CRM, a branded client portal and mobile app, workflows, billing and proposals, plus a Bookkeeping Hub that connects client ledgers and manages uncategorized transactions. It prices by active clients and bills annually: from $1,500 a year at the 150-client minimum (about $0.83 per client a month), with 20 seats included and volume bands above 150. Firms look elsewhere when they want monthly billing, a lower total for a tiny client list, shared-email triage, or month-end close on Xero as well as QBO. These are the closest options in our directory, not a full market scan.</p>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Alternative</th>
        <th>Best fit vs TaxDome</th>
        <th>Pricing (verified Nov 2026)</th>
        <th>Trade-off</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><a href={`${b}/tools/karbon`}>Karbon</a></td>
        <td>Teams that run client work out of shared email and want it turned into tasks, with AI email summaries, and prefer monthly billing (teams of 4+)</td>
        <td>Team $59/user/mo; Business $89/user/mo (annual); monthly $79/$99 only for teams of 4+</td>
        <td>No Bookkeeping Hub for uncategorized QBO transactions; no branded client mobile app like TaxDome</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><a href={`${b}/tools/financial-cents`}>Financial Cents</a></td>
        <td>Solo and small QBO firms that want workflows, client chasing and billing at a lower seat price, plus an optional close add-on</td>
        <td>Solo $19/mo; Team $49/user/mo; Scale $69/user/mo (annual); Month-End Close add-on $5/client/mo</td>
        <td>Close review is a paid per-client add-on (QBO only); lighter on tax organizers and IRS tools</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><a href={`${b}/tools/double`}>Double</a></td>
        <td>Bookkeeping firms whose bottleneck is month-end close and client file review on QBO or Xero, not a full tax-and-bookkeeping portal</td>
        <td>Per connected client on Core, Plus, Scale and Enterprise tiers; prices not published, demo first</td>
        <td>A close and client review tool, not full practice management: no firm-wide client portal, tax organizers or time-and-billing like TaxDome</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Cost for a 3-person firm with 20 clients (list prices, per month)</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>TaxDome: $1,500 per year at the 150-client minimum (~$125 per month), billed annually, 20 seats included. Under 150 active clients you still pay the 150 minimum.</li>
    <li>Karbon: 3 × $59 = $177 (Team, annual) or 3 × $89 = $267 (Business, annual). A 3-person team cannot pay monthly.</li>
    <li>Financial Cents: 3 × $49 = $147 (Team, annual), or $247 with the close add-on for 20 clients (20 × $5).</li>
    <li>Double: not published.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>When to stay on TaxDome</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You also do tax work and want organizers, IRS transcripts and return delivery in the same portal as bookkeeping.</li>
    <li>Your month-end bottleneck is getting clients to explain uncategorized QBO transactions, and you want that inside the same portal.</li>
    <li>You want a branded client portal and mobile app, and you are fine paying annually.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>FAQ</h2>
  {faqs.map(([q, a]) => (<><h3>{q}</h3><p>{a}</p></>))}
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={faqLd} />

  <p>Sources: taxdome.com/pricing checked 2026-11-06; karbonhq.com/pricing, financial-cents.com/pricing and doublehq.com/pricing checked earlier Oct 2026 sessions. No sponsor has paid for this comparison.</p>

  <p>
    <a href={`${b}/tools/taxdome`}>TaxDome</a>
    · <a href={`${b}/compare/taxdome-vs-karbon`}>TaxDome vs Karbon</a>
    · <a href={`${b}/compare/karbon-alternatives`}>Karbon alternatives</a>
    · <a href={`${b}/compare/financial-cents-alternatives`}>Financial Cents alternatives</a>
    · <a href={`${b}/category/practice-management`}>All practice management tools</a>
  </p>
</Base>

<style>
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 1rem 0; font-size: 0.95rem; }
  th, td { border: 1px solid #ddd; padding: 0.5rem 0.6rem; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }
  th { background: #f6f6f6; }
</style>
